tion":0.06613097242214093,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.06689,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":44.6,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"MACOM Technology Solutions Holdings, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, provides analog semiconductor solutions for use in wireless and wireline applications across the radio frequency (RF), microwave, millimeter wave, and lightwave spectrum. The company offers a portfolio of standard and custom devices, including integrated circuits, multi-chip modules, diodes, amplifiers, switches and switch limiters, passive and active components, and subsystems. Its semiconductor products are electronic components that are incorporated into electronic systems, such as wireless base stations, optical networks, radar and medical systems, satellite networks, and test and measurement applications. The company serves carrier infrastructure, which comprise long-haul/metro, 5G and 6G infrastructure, satellite communications, and fiber-to-the-X/passive optical network; industrial and defense, including military and commercial radar, RF jammers, electronic countermeasures, and communication data links, as well as multi-market applications, such as industrial, medical, test and measurement, and scientific applications; and data centers. It sells its products through direct sales force, applications engineering staff, independent sales representatives, resellers, and distributors. The company operates in the United States, China, Japan, Singapore, South Korea, Taiwan, and internationally. MACOM Technology Solutions Holdings, Inc. was formerly known as M/A-Com Technology Solutions Holdings, Inc. and changed its name to MACOM Technology Solutions Holdings, Inc. in 2016. MACOM Technology Solutions Holdings, Inc. was founded in 1950 and is based in Lowell, Massachusetts.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Stephen G. Daly | President, CEO & Chairman | Age 59 | Compensation: $2.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["MACOM Technology Solutions Hold is a large-cap technology business with a $17.7B market cap on $1.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +27% over the past three years and +9% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 13% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically. Gross margins of 51% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $293M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 22 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.07\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 48\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.3%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 6.7% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 175% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.746486159241794},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $17.1M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (38% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"AI disruption of existing software moats \u2014 incumbents with durable margins face commoditisation as AI-native competitors replicate features at a fraction of the R&D cost.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 16% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Growing faster than most Technology peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"M/A-Com (MTSI) International Revenue Performance Explored","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3029378/m-a-com-mtsi-international-revenue-performance-explored?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cnfm_international_revenues-3029378","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794575712.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Discipline and Rules-Based Execution in MTSI Response","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/15/Discipline_and_Rules-Based_Execution_in_MTSI_Response_111226024802_1794512882.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794512882.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.178,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Wells Fargo & Company (NYSE:WFC) Stock Purchase Disclosed by Rep. Gilbert Ray Cisneros, Jr.","so